{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/tuikit\/statusbarguide"]}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The status bar is a row at the bottom of the terminal that shows keyboard shortcuts and contextual information. It updates every frame while it has active items."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The status bar is hidden automatically when there are no active user items and no visible system items."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"TUIkit provides two status bar styles: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarStyle\/compact","type":"reference"},{"text":" (single-line, shortcuts only) and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarStyle\/bordered","type":"reference"},{"text":" (bordered with title support).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Architecture","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Architecture"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The status bar system has three parts:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarState"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Manages the item stack, style, and event handling"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarItem","type":"reference","isActive":true}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":": A single shortcut entry (key + label + action)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBar","isActive":true}]},{"text":": The view that renders items into a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FrameBuffer"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Defining-Status-Bar-Items","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Defining Status Bar Items"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"code":"statusBarItems","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier on your views to register shortcuts:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["VStack {","    Text(\"My App\")","}",".statusBarItems {","    StatusBarItem(shortcut: \"n\", label: \"new\") {","        \/\/ handle \"n\" key press","    }","    StatusBarItem(shortcut: \"d\", label: \"delete\") {","        \/\/ handle \"d\" key press","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Items are registered per frame during rendering. When a view is removed from the tree, its items automatically disappear from the status bar."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Shortcut-Display-Symbols","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Shortcut Display Symbols"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Shortcut"},{"text":" to keep displayed shortcut symbols consistent:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Constant","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Display","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Description","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Shortcut.quit"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Default quit display"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Shortcut.enter","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"↵"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Enter \/ Return"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Shortcut.escape"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"⎋"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Escape"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Shortcut.tab","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"⇥","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tab"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Shortcut.arrowUp","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"↑","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Arrow up"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Shortcut.arrowDown"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"↓"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Arrow down","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Shortcut.arrowsUpDown","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"↑↓"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertical navigation","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Shortcut.ctrl(\"q\")"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"⌃q"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ctrl+Q display"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Shortcut"},{"type":"text","text":" defines how the item is displayed. If you do not pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"key:"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StatusBarItem"},{"type":"text","text":" derives a trigger key from the shortcut string where possible."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Context-Stack","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Context Stack"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Status bar items use a "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"context stack"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":". Context-specific items can temporarily replace global items, for example while a dialog is visible:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Dialog(title: \"Confirm\") {","    Text(\"Delete file?\")","} footer: {","    ButtonRow {","        Button(\"Delete\") { delete() }","        Button(\"Cancel\") { cancel() }","    }","}",".statusBarItems(context: \"confirm-dialog\") {","    StatusBarItem(shortcut: \"y\", label: \"yes\") { delete() }","    StatusBarItem(shortcut: \"n\", label: \"no\") { cancel() }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The topmost context replaces global user items in the display. System items remain visible unless a user item uses the same shortcut string."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"System-Items","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"System Items"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"TUIkit registers built-in system items automatically:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Key"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Label"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Action"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Quit"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exit the application"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Appearance"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cycle to next border appearance"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"t"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Theme"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Cycle to next color theme"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"These appear on the right side of the status bar. Only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q quit"},{"type":"text","text":" is shown by default. Enable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"a appearance"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"t theme"},{"type":"text","text":" with the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/View\/statusBarSystemItems(theme:appearance:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" modifier."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Overriding-q-quit","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Overriding `q quit`"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A user-defined status bar item with shortcut ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" overrides the built-in quit binding for that view context:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["EditorView()","    .statusBarItems {","        StatusBarItem(shortcut: \"q\", label: \"close\") {","            closeEditor()","        }","    }"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This works because status bar items with actions are handled before the default quit binding. The built-in "},{"code":"q quit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" system item is also removed from the display when a user item uses the same shortcut string."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Changing-the-global-quit-shortcut","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Changing the global quit shortcut"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Change the built-in quit key through "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarState\/quitShortcut","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    @Environment(\\.statusBar) private var statusBar","","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","        }","        .task {","            statusBar.quitShortcut = .escape","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Available presets include "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/QuitShortcut\/q"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/QuitShortcut\/escape"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/QuitShortcut\/ctrlQ"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/QuitShortcut\/ctrlC"},{"type":"text","text":". You can also create a fully custom "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/QuitShortcut"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Hiding-the-status-bar-completely","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Hiding the status bar completely"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hide all system items and do not register any user items:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["ContentView()","    .statusBarSystemItems(theme: false, appearance: false)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"code":["@Environment(\\.statusBar) private var statusBar","","statusBar.showSystemItems = false"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When there are no active items left, the status bar height becomes zero and it is not rendered."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Status-Bar-Styles","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Status Bar Styles"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Two styles are available:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBar